1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,895
Can one CSV file become an Excel workbook,
a slide deck, a Word report,

2
00:00:06,895 --> 00:00:09,814
and a PDF handout, all done by AI?

3
00:00:09,814 --> 00:00:15,136
This video introduces Anthropic's four
official Office skills.

4
00:00:16,100 --> 00:00:20,514
Without skills, the AI often writes
throwaway code to read files,

5
00:00:20,514 --> 00:00:22,687
breaks when formats get complex,

6
00:00:22,687 --> 00:00:26,965
and produces Excel files and slides with
content but no layout.

7
00:00:26,965 --> 00:00:30,700
With skills, it follows an officially
curated workflow,

8
00:00:30,700 --> 00:00:34,843
and even renders slides as images to check
the layout itself.

9
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,141
Each skill handles one file type.

10
00:00:38,141 --> 00:00:42,895
docx covers Word headings, tables of
contents, and tracked changes;

11
00:00:42,895 --> 00:00:47,152
pdf extracts text, merges and splits
files, and fills forms;

12
00:00:47,152 --> 00:00:51,834
pptx handles layout, charts, and
animation; xlsx handles formulas,

13
00:00:51,834 --> 00:00:53,466
formatting, and charts.

14
00:00:53,466 --> 00:00:55,452
You don't need to name them:

15
00:00:55,452 --> 00:00:59,709
they load automatically whenever a task
touches these files.

16
00:01:00,667 --> 00:01:03,904
Before installing, open the right folder:
use Open

17
00:01:03,904 --> 00:01:07,076
Folder on the Unit 03 folder, not the
outer one.

18
00:01:07,076 --> 00:01:11,327
Then install the four skills in the
terminal with npx skills add.

19
00:01:11,327 --> 00:01:16,297
After installing, always start a new
conversation so the skills take effect.

20
00:01:17,233 --> 00:01:19,050
You also need three tools.

21
00:01:19,050 --> 00:01:21,775
uv and Node.js let the skills run code.

22
00:01:21,775 --> 00:01:25,339
LibreOffice recalculates formulas,
converts to PDF,

23
00:01:25,339 --> 00:01:28,554
and lets the AI see what the slides look
like.

24
00:01:28,554 --> 00:01:31,069
Finally, open the results in Office:

25
00:01:31,069 --> 00:01:35,192
animations and transitions are most
accurate in PowerPoint.

26
00:01:36,133 --> 00:01:41,041
There's just one sample dataset: Taiwan's
Purchasing Managers' Index,

27
00:01:41,041 --> 00:01:44,099
with monthly PMI and NMI from 2012 to
2026.

28
00:01:44,099 --> 00:01:49,718
The four examples form a pipeline: each
step's output is the next step's input.

29
00:01:50,667 --> 00:01:56,107
Example one uses xlsx to turn the CSV into
Excel: one sheet holds the raw data,

30
00:01:56,107 --> 00:02:00,995
another computes the yearly averages, and
a line chart shows the trend.

31
00:02:00,995 --> 00:02:05,678
Click a cell, and you should see a
formula, not a hard-coded number.

32
00:02:06,633 --> 00:02:11,676
Example two uses pptx to build a
five-slide deck from the Excel file.

33
00:02:11,676 --> 00:02:15,914
The prompt is very specific: editable
text, a card layout,

34
00:02:15,914 --> 00:02:21,103
one card fading in per click, slow fade
transitions, and speaker notes.

35
00:02:22,067 --> 00:02:24,036
Then check it in PowerPoint.

36
00:02:24,036 --> 00:02:28,676
Only the cards are animated, and one more
appears with each click;

37
00:02:28,676 --> 00:02:34,231
transitions are longer than the default
0.7 seconds; and every slide has notes.

38
00:02:34,231 --> 00:02:39,223
Animations and transitions must be written
directly into the slide XML,

39
00:02:39,223 --> 00:02:42,668
and that's exactly where the pptx skill
comes in.

40
00:02:43,633 --> 00:02:48,266
Example three uses docx to write a Word
report from the same Excel file,

41
00:02:48,266 --> 00:02:52,706
with a cover page, an automatic table of
contents, and four chapters.

42
00:02:52,706 --> 00:02:57,596
Right after it's generated, the table of
contents may be empty: right-click,

43
00:02:57,596 --> 00:03:00,749
choose Update Field, and the page numbers
appear.

44
00:03:01,700 --> 00:03:04,618
Finally, pdf turns the report into a
handout,

45
00:03:04,618 --> 00:03:08,443
with page numbers and a light gray
watermark on every page.

46
00:03:08,443 --> 00:03:12,138
The most common mistake is not specifying
a Chinese font,

47
00:03:12,138 --> 00:03:15,315
so the watermark turns into boxes; when it
works,

48
00:03:15,315 --> 00:03:17,649
the Chinese text displays correctly.

49
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:23,742
One CSV, four skills: from Excel and
slides all the way to Word and PDF.

50
00:03:23,742 --> 00:03:27,130
Open the right folder, install the skills,
start

51
00:03:27,130 --> 00:03:29,883
a new conversation, and give it a try.

